WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:02.760
- All right, Norman.
- Yes sir.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:03.900
- [Mark] Welcome back.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:04.733
- Glad to be back.

00:00:04.733 --> 00:00:05.566
- [Mark] So where are we at today?

00:00:05.566 --> 00:00:06.870
You started to work about a week ago.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:07.703
- Yes.

00:00:07.703 --> 00:00:08.870
Started work a week ago.

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:10.213
I'm a retail associate.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.320
Got a nice little promotion
last night as a floor leader.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.600
- You got a promotion?
- Yes.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.410
- That's great.
- Yeah.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:19.210
They just seen to leadership ability

00:00:20.058 --> 00:00:22.360
and the knack for knowing
exactly what to do

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:24.363
how to do it, where to place things.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.480
It's quite different
than what I'm used to.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.620
I've never been a retail associate.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:31.820
You know, a nice little
title but I'll take it.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.093
And so it's a wonderful company.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:37.010
Damn good benefits.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:39.760
They got a lot of things in
there and I really enjoy it,

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.550
really, really enjoy it.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.062
- [Mark] That's excellent.

00:00:43.062 --> 00:00:45.470
So you're staying with your friend Don?

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.350
- Yes, my best buddy.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:48.337
- [Mark] And how is that?

00:00:48.337 --> 00:00:50.780
How was he, so Don uses?

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:51.613
- Yeah.

00:00:51.613 --> 00:00:52.710
- [Mark] And you're using or not?

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:53.640
- No.
- You're not?

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:54.911
- No.

00:00:54.911 --> 00:00:55.744
- [Mark] And like you mentioned before

00:00:55.744 --> 00:00:57.690
Don kind of like goes somewhere else and -

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.100
- The degree of respectability

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.420
that he has for me and what I'm doing

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.430
and what I'm trying my best to do,

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.410
is it's an insurmountable.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:07.420
I mean, he's a great person

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:10.980
and it doesn't bother me
that he does what he does.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.700
You know, this is my friend.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.420
Friend is a hell of a word.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:15.630
You know you can have an associate

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:18.600
you can have a partner,
but he's my friend,

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.170
because when I really needed
some help, he was right there.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.757
You know, no strings attached,

00:01:24.757 --> 00:01:26.620
"Hey man this is what you need?

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.270
Come on."

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.690
And of course in my mind

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.170
I would like him to follow my path.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.660
But in your own way,

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:37.320
you know it happens in different times.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.730
I think I quoted a scripture once

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.467
before the Ecclesiastics 3:1

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:43.160
"A time and a purpose and
a season for everything."

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.270
You know, it's not his time,

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.530
maybe it's not the purpose.

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:47.830
It's not his season.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:49.350
Maybe it's mine and made me by me

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:51.070
going through what I'm going through

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:53.639
to get where I wanna get,

00:01:53.639 --> 00:01:54.750
will you know,

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:58.530
somehow pull him, you
know, he's his own man.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:01:59.650
He's a grown man, you know?

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:01.950
And then decisions are
made by yourself, you know

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:03.650
power, choice and control.

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:06.170
You lose one, you lose them all.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:08.080
That's just my own philosophy.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:10.150
So it'll happen for him.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:11.250
- Yeah.
- I know it will.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.320
- [Mark] Have you wrapped
your head around the concept

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.680
that relapses are just
part of the process?

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:16.513
- Yes.

00:02:16.513 --> 00:02:17.421
- [Mark] And there may be more.

00:02:17.421 --> 00:02:19.120
- There may be more who knows

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:24.090
but I no longer suffer
from that impending doom.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.440
I don't even count my days anymore.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:29.680
When I go to work and I go home,

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:31.587
I rest, I wake up, when I wake up I say,

00:02:31.587 --> 00:02:33.510
"Thank you for this day."

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:36.260
Because I don't wanna put
too much pressure on myself.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:38.420
Not so much that I know myself.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.230
I am beginning to know a little bit more

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:43.923
about the power and the
insidiousness of the disease.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:47.460
Everything will be fine

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:51.330
not a cloud on the horizon,
(snaps finger) just like that.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:52.570
A lot of people don't understand that.

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:54.220
And they say, "Why?"

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.690
Well if we could answer the question, why

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:59.430
then probably a lot of
people would be sober

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.280
and wouldn't do what they do.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.450
And a lot of people wouldn't do

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.933
the other things that they
do beyond drugs and alcohol.

00:03:03.933 --> 00:03:06.764
- [Mark] Yes and sometimes
its something stressful

00:03:06.764 --> 00:03:09.674
but also sometimes it's something
positive will trigger it.

00:03:09.674 --> 00:03:10.507
- Right.

00:03:10.507 --> 00:03:13.178
- [Mark] Is it the inability to accept

00:03:13.178 --> 00:03:15.700
the fortune that you just came across?

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:16.570
- Well no, you know what?

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:17.560
I really don't know.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.360
I can't answer that question.

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:20.500
I had actually, you know

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:24.380
because I prided myself on
knowing a lot of things.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:26.240
I actually went to my boss.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.330
I think it was Tuesday night.

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:31.073
And I told him, I don't know.

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:33.450
And that was humbling for me

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:37.860
because usually Norman
knows, but I didn't know.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.280
And it wasn't a point of me

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:42.713
being scared or something
like that of asking him.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:44.710
But I thought to myself,

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:46.830
when I tried something three times,

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.460
I said, you know what, go to the boss.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:49.660
- [Mark] This is something
pertaining to work?

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:51.010
- Yes and I just went.

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:54.317
- [Mark] I love somebody who
will tell me, I don't know

00:03:54.317 --> 00:03:56.660
so much better than somebody
pretending like they do.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:59.580
- And what they do, is
they say ask questions

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:00.757
and they'll always, they'll come around,

00:04:00.757 --> 00:04:01.637
"Hey, Norman, are you all right?"

00:04:01.637 --> 00:04:02.787
"Yeah, sure."

00:04:02.787 --> 00:04:03.620
"Everything's fine?"

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:04.453
"Yeah, sure."

00:04:04.453 --> 00:04:05.910
Then they'll audit you.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.333
Now, I'm running around with a scanner,

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:10.540
but they can tap into my scanner

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:11.690
and find everything that I'm doing.

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:13.180
And at the end of the night,

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:16.750
they say who's made a mistake,
who put something wrong

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:18.760
and they look at the percentage as well.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:20.610
I've done quite well.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.750
I've scored a hundred percent every night

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:24.970
because I pride myself in doing my best.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:28.040
And it's a new experience and learning.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:32.000
So the newness really really motivates me

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.870
because it's something new
and I like to learn things.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:36.700
So it's pretty cool.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:37.680
I enjoy it.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:38.513
I enjoy it.

00:04:38.513 --> 00:04:41.910
And we're gonna take in one day at a time.

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:43.640
We're not looking forward

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:44.680
because there's some other things

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:47.010
that they told me last
night that could come down.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:48.900
And I'm not looking at that.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:51.200
No, stay right here.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.420
Do what you have to do.

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:53.730
And just keep pushing.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:54.840
Just take it a day at a time.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:56.820
You don't have to look at
what's gonna happen in a month.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:57.840
You don't have to think about

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.480
what's gonna happen in a month.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:01.550
Just keep going.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.070
Take it a day at a time.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:05.160
Go to work, go on your break

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:08.200
go back to work, go to lunch, go to work

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:13.200
go on your break, go home,
rest, be ready for the next day.

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:18.270
- [Mark] And trying to break
a crack cocaine addiction

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:21.680
without rehab will be quite a feat, right?

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:25.880
- Well, I know a lot of
people who didn't go to rehab.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:28.820
I know a lot of people who
went the religious route

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:31.630
I know a lot of people that
just stopped cold turkey.

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:33.160
It takes what it takes for a person.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:34.430
You know, like I've said before,

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.600
I've been in 50 something rehabs.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.230
And a lot of people had
commented on that too

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.500
on the page and you know,
some good and some bad.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:42.700
And that was okay.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:47.690
But you know, it's
really on the individual.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:50.610
It doesn't matter where you go.

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:53.120
Okay a treatment facility
and we'll do one,

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.000
a couple of things.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.520
It'll house you, that's one,

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:57.800
if you're homeless.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:58.973
Two, it'll feed you.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:03.540
Some have donated clothes
so it'll cloth you,

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:05.770
but why am I in that rehab?

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:06.930
Why did I go to treatment?

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:11.050
Did I really go to this
facility to seek treatment?

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:13.540
Or was it the fact that
everything got a real bad?

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:14.530
I robbed somebody,

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:16.810
I'm running from the law
and let me get in here

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:19.400
so I can get a paper
sign and go to the court.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.810
And they say, Oh, you're in
rehab, everything's fine.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:23.013
It's on the person.

00:06:23.898 --> 00:06:24.890
What do you wanna do?

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.820
Do you really need treatment.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:27.960
So there was some people that commented

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:29.930
on the page that said, "I needed to get

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:32.160
out of the Skid Row area
and go to treatment."

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.740
Well, guess what?

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:35.730
Skid Row is just not a place.

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:36.683
It's a mentality.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.230
That's my own philosophy.

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:41.100
You can be living in Beverly Hills

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.980
with a Skid Row mentality.

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:44.540
You can be living in Playa Vista,

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:47.440
you can be living in these
wonderful communities

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.090
but you can have a Skid Row mentality.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:51.300
So it's just not a place.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.400
And guess what?

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.840
If I go to the treatment
center, who am I taking with me?

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:55.970
Me.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:57.970
If I leave down from Skid Row

00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:00.113
and go to another state who's taking me?

00:07:00.113 --> 00:07:02.300
I'm still there.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:03.980
So and for me, the kind of (indistinct)

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:06.340
and I wouldn't give a where it's at.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:09.103
If I'm going to Alaska,
I'm going to ask Eskimo.

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:14.200
So it really doesn't matter where you go.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:18.190
Do you have the wherewithal
to say within yourself

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:19.260
I'm tired of this.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:20.590
I want something better.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:22.360
Today, I do.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:23.780
I don't know about tomorrow.

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:25.120
I don't know about the next day

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.730
but today right now as I'm speaking.

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:29.650
Yeah, I have the wherewithal

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:31.250
this is what I would like to do.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:33.510
- [Mark] Excellent.

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:34.750
I wish you the best of luck.

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:36.840
Continue your forward progress.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:37.673
- Thank you, sir.

00:07:37.673 --> 00:07:39.210
Always a pleasure.

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:40.420
- [Mark] Do another
update in a week or two?

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:41.253
- Yes, sir.

00:07:41.253 --> 00:07:42.086
- All right.
- Okay.

00:07:42.086 --> 00:07:42.919
- [Mark] Thanks.

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:46.167
- Damn I kinda listened to
myself on that one (laughs).

